WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.480
Hold a flame to a ball of cotton.

2
00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:03.660
It burns.

3
00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:05.020
Every time.

4
00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:07.120
But what do you actually see?

5
00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:10.240
Al-Ghazali said: burning with the contact,

6
00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:11.640
not through it.

7
00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:14.280
The Qur'an makes a
different kind of claim.

8
00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:17.670
It challenges readers to
produce a surah like it.

9
00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:20.900
And Muslim mystics seek
to know God directly.

10
00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:24.310
Al-Ghazali called it
tasting, not argument.

11
00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:27.270
So how would anyone test a Muslim claim?

12
00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:31.630
In this mission, you'll compare the
revelation of the Qur'an with the experience

13
00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:32.780
of mystics.

14
00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:37.530
Then you'll put al-Ghazali and
David Hume side by side on causes,

15
00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:40.010
miracles and rival religions.

16
00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:44.360
Your mission: work out how different
Muslim claims could be tested.
